  "description": "#6559 — page mode sends its creates as one `create_blocks_batch` under the ids its document gave them, and its deletes as one `delete_blocks_by_ids`. A spec's client id is taken verbatim, a later spec may sit under an earlier one's, and an id a block holds (live or trashed) or an earlier spec took rolls the whole batch back with `conflict`, as `create_block` refuses it. S7, S8 and S9 are purged first, so no row holds their ids. A batch delete stamps every root with one `deleted_at`, and a `restore_block` with it brings back that one root's cohort, not the other roots'.",
